  <h2>Frequently asked questions about home construction companies in Lucknow</h2>

  <h3>How do I verify if a home construction company in Lucknow is genuine?</h3>

  <p>Ask for their GSTIN, MSME Udyam registration number, and ISO certificate. Then ask to visit at least one completed project and one ongoing site. A genuine company will provide all of these without hesitation. VP Infra is MSME-registered (UDYAM-UP-50-0085926) and ISO 9001:2015 certified, with active project sites open to prospective clients on request.</p>

  <h3>What is the typical construction timeline for a G+1 home in Lucknow?</h3>

  <p>A well-managed G+1 residential project in Lucknow takes 14 to 18 months from foundation to handover. The grey structure alone takes 6 to 9 months. Delays happen most often when procurement is disorganised or when a client changes the design mid-project. Milestone-based scheduling with weekly progress reports, which VP Infra follows on every project, keeps this on track.</p>

  <h3>Is an ISO-certified construction company more expensive?</h3>

  <p>Not necessarily. ISO 9001:2015 certification audits a company's process quality, not its pricing. What it does mean is that the company has documented procedures for material testing, site management, and client communication. In practice, this reduces costly rework and delays, which can save you money even if the per-square-foot rate is slightly higher than an uncertified contractor.</p>

